  "text": "Zoe (Design): quick one from usability: Cmd/Ctrl+K focuses search but VoiceOver reads the input twice. Repro: Cmd+K -> VO: 'Search' then 'Search' again.\nIrfan (Frontend): thanks, I can repro. DOM has visible <label> + input aria-label. Likely double-source name.\nMaya (A11y): yep. Fix: remove aria-label and use aria-labelledby pointing at the label id. If we need extra context for SR, add a sr-only span inside the label (eg 'Search Redwood Console').\nIrfan (Frontend): ok will change to <label id=\"top-search\">Search <span class=\"sr-only\">Search Redwood Console</span></label>\n<input aria-labelledby=\"top-search\" placeholder=\"Search\" /> and remove aria-label.\nKai (QA): I'll add a smoke test: trigger shortcut, ensure screen reader output contains single 'Search Redwood Console, edit text'. Also check Windows/NVDA parity.\nZoe (Design): also note focus ring on dark theme is thin; prefer 3px outline + subtle halo. Small CSS to include in PR.\nIrfan (Frontend): will include :focus-visible { outline:3px solid #60a5fa; outline-offset:2px; box-shadow:0 0 0 4px rgba(96,165,250,0.08); } in the change.\nMaya (A11y): one last nit: when opening suggestions announce counts in a polite region, but debounce updates so it doesn't speak on every keystroke. Owners: Irfan (PR), Maya (a11y review), Kai (QA). Target: patch this week. :thumbsup:"
}